From bd01a0817b1b186077cd2cab5524e2455724a24f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gargrohin <29701609+gargrohin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:31:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Add RoboTwin aloha_agilex action-policy dataset and SFT
 wrapper

RoboTwinLeRobotDataset reads the LeRobot v2.1 RoboTwin layout directly
(per-episode parquet + AV1 mp4, one instruction per episode) and emits the
DROID joint_pos + use_state contract: 14-D absolute joint positions with the
current state as a clean conditioning row, quantile-normalized from a stats
JSON. The three cameras are composed AgiBot-style (head on top, both wrists
at half size below, 360x320). The flat frame index is cached in an .npz
because reading 12,500 parquet files from EFS takes minutes per rank, and
each worker decodes a whole episode once since the shuffle stream reads
windows sequentially within an episode.

get_action_robotwin_sft_dataset wraps it in ActionTransformPipeline with
resolution pinned to "256" (auto-detect would choose the 480 tier for a
360x320 canvas).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
